@startuml codeemb-pooling
' How a rank-3 hidden-state tensor [1, L, d] is collapsed to a single d-vector.
' The three shipped embedders disagree: CodeT5+ mean-pools over the sequence axis,
' UniXcoder and GraphCodeBERT take the CLS row. A rank-2 output is passed through.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-pooling.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 3 in docs/components/code-embeddings/overview.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Pooling — collapsing hidden states H ∈ ℝ^(L×d) to one vector

rectangle "**ONNX output tensor**\nshape_dims = shape.iter()" as t #2E7D32

rectangle "**rank 2** → [1, d]\nalready pooled by the graph\n(CodeT5+ embedding export)" as r2 #388E3C
rectangle "**rank 3** → [1, L, d]\nper-token hidden states H\n(encoder last_hidden_state)" as r3 #388E3C
rectangle "**any other rank**\nCodeEmbeddingError::Inference" as rx #90A4AE

rectangle "**CLS pooling**\nv = H₀ (row of the first token)\ndata[..hidden_dim]" as cls #1B5E20
rectangle "**Mean pooling**\nv = (1∕L) · Σ_{i=0}^{L−1} Hᵢ" as mean #1B5E20

rectangle "**UniXcoder**\n**GraphCodeBERT**" as ug #43A047
rectangle "**CodeT5+**" as ct #43A047

rectangle "**v ∈ ℝᵈ**  → L2 normalize" as out #455A64

t --> r2
t --> r3
t --> rx : error
r2 --> out : pass through
r3 --> cls
r3 --> mean
cls --> ug
mean --> ct
ug --> out
ct --> out

note right of mean #E8F5E9
  The mean is taken over **every** row,
  the attention mask is not applied.
  Sound only because the batch axis is
  fixed at 1, so no padding row exists.
end note

note left of cls #E8F5E9
  CLS row = ⟨s⟩ / [CLS], the position the
  RoBERTa-family sentence objective was
  trained to summarize the input into.
end note

@enduml
